    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Ferroelectricity is a property where materials contain spontaneous, polarization states that can be aligned in the same direction by a built-in electric field. When combined with photovoltaic devices this ferroelectric response can improve charge carrier separation and increase photovoltaic efficiency.  When spin-orbit coupling effects, such as the Rashba effect, are also present in a material, an additional level of control over optoelectronic properties is offered in comparison to an ordinary ferroelectric system. These materials, known as Ferroelectric Rashba semiconductors (FERSCs), include noncentrosymmetric two-dimensional hybrid perovskites (2DHPs), which are promising candidates for applications in retinomorphic technologies and spintronic devices. In this work, we probe for the Rashba effect in noncentrosymmetric 2DHPs with the formula (2-FBZ)₂(A)ₙ₋₁PbₙI₃ₙ₊₁ (2-FBZ = 2-fluorobenzylammonium, A designates organic cations including FA = formamidinium and MA = methylammonium) by probing for a helicity-dependent response. Our results indicate no change in response in all three 2DHPs as there is little difference in THz signals from exposure to right vs left circularly polarized light. A lack of helicity-dependence also indicates absence of the Rashba effect, meaning emitted THz fields may originate from out of plane currents generated by trivial effects including Dember fields, band bending, and optical rectification. Further work entails degradation studies of the 2DHPs under varying fluence, measurements with a half wave plate to probe for the presence of optical rectification, and measurements with vertical wire-grid polarizer orientation for maximized detection of in-plane induced current responses.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
